      "summary": "feat/library-export-enhancement: add web song browser export (#1540)",
      "description": "* feat(song): add web song browser export\n\nAdd a self-contained HTML song browser export for sharing song libraries\noutside of YARG. A fourth \"Web Page\" button in Settings > File Management >\nExport Songs generates a single HTML file with all data embedded, written\nvia a streaming template approach (Seg0/DATA/Seg1/GENRES/Seg2/META/Seg3)\nso the full document is never materialized in memory.\n\nCore features:\n- Compact JSON schema with interned genres and base-36 difficulty encoding\n  (5-char VGDKB code: '.' absent, '?' unknown tier, 0-9a-z otherwise)\n- Virtualized row rendering for large libraries (5000+ songs)\n- Bottom sheet detail view with per-instrument difficulty tiers\n- Filter chips for instrument parts (V/G/D/K/B) with brand colors\n- Gear-icon search settings with per-field toggles (artist/title/album)\n- Clickable column headers for sorting (artist default ascending)\n- Dark/light theme with sun/moon toggle and localStorage persistence\n- Progressive mobile column hiding (3 breakpoints)\n- V->H badge for harmony songs, grey dash for absent instruments\n- Difficulty tier display with numeric prefix and tier-based coloring\n- Vocal parts: 'N Harmony Parts' / 'Solo Vocals' / 'None'\n\nThe HTML/CSS/JS template is embedded in WebBrowserTemplate.cs as a verbatim\nstring (LF line endings inside the literal; do not reformat) and split at\nstatic init around the three substitution markers, with fail-fast marker\nvalidation. The DATA and GENRES payloads escape '<' to \\u003C so\nuser-controlled song metadata cannot terminate the inline script block.\nWebBrowserRecord is a plain class rather than a record because Unity's\nruntime lacks the IsExternalInit shim required by init accessors.\n\n* refactor(song): move exporters into Song/Exporters subfolder\n\nReview feedback on #1540: group the export scripts (SongExport,\nOuvertExport, and the new WebBrowser* files) under a dedicated\nAssets/Script/Song/Exporters/ folder, with a matching\nYARG.Song.Exporters namespace.\n\nAlso adds the .cs.meta files for the new WebBrowser* scripts, which\nwere missing from the original commit.\n\n* fix(song): polish length column in web export\n\nSort-by-length arrow overlapped the YEAR header (fixed 50px track too\nnarrow for LENGTH + indicator): Length -> 62px, Year -> 44px across\nthe base layout and responsive breakpoints.\n\nRight-align times with tabular figures and 1ch right padding so the\ncolon stays put between 9:59 and 10:00+ and the value doesn't crowd\nthe year column."
